WEBVTT

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:10.990
I must've fallen asleep.

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.150
Who's there?

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:16.450
Yakumo-kun?

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.700
Yakumo's safe.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:19.830
What?

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.120
I've got a message for you from him.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.790
"Don't slack off on your concert practices."

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:29.340
Who are you?

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.260
Where's Yakumo-kun?

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:33.470
Please tell me!

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.470
I'm begging you!

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:38.180
He's in Nagano.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.930
There are people after you.

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:44.980
Don't be rash. Wait for Yakumo to return.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:46.940
Wait!

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:12.460
Azusa, you're a weak woman.

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:14.920
You still fear me even after your death.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.890
You're still unable to show yourself to me.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:20.390
You can watch from here

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:26.390
as Yakumo is engulfed by the darkness.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:28.690
How are you doing, Makoto-san?

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:31.650
There's nothing suspicious so far.

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:37.950
Perhaps Detective Goto's disappearance was unrelated to the Nanase Murders after all.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:40.200
It's still too early to draw any conclusions.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:43.080
If there aren't any clues in the reports,

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:47.920
then we still have one more avenue left to explore: the coroner for the autopsies, Hata-sensei.

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:02.470
Excuse me, but when can you show us the files?

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:05.060
Right after I finish this.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.100
And that is?

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:10.860
I'm attempting to make a facial construction of what the missing girl, Nanase Miyuki,

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:13.070
would look like today.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:18.450
Although the Forensic Laboratory can produce a construction using various algorithms,

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.280
my simulation program incorporates my imagination into the construction as well.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:24.660
I call it Hobby Simulation.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:31.380
I imagine that after experiencing 15 years of ruin, she'd resemble Death.

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:35.590
That's... Hoshino Yukiko.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:41.010
Wait a minute. I think I've seen her somewhere before.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.850
Oh! I remember!

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.350
Look at this.

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:51.850
Although Yakumo-kun and that idiot Goto visited me separately a few days ago,

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:54.610
they both had the same reaction upon seeing this photo and rushed out.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:02:59.530
Ishii-san!

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:07.870
I'm positive there's some kind of connection between

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:11.620
Detective Goto, Yakumo-shi, and Hoshino Yukiko-No, Nanase Miyuki.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.040
We're not returning to the police station?

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:19.220
Nanase Miyuki's grade school teacher is named in the investigation reports.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.220
Let's question her.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:31.440
Let's see... At the time, I felt that Miyuki-san was being neglected by her family.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:37.900
Why that's a rather mysterious room, isn't it?

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:41.400
It's a secret room my father built.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:46.410
He built it so that he could <i>play</i> with me there.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:52.790
No such room was mentioned in the reports.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:56.040
Maybe that's where Detective Goto is being held.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:58.630
Most likely.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:08.890
Ishii-san, look...

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:15.310
What was that just now?

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:17.270
I don't know.

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:35.080
So this is...

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:37.710
the secret room.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:47.850
Detective Goto!

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:50.260
I'm glad that you're safe.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.270
Thank goodness. I'm really glad.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:56.900
Don't just sit around, you idiot!

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:59.020
Yakumo and Haruka-chan are in danger!

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:00.940
Yes, this is Ozawa.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:02.690
Oh? Mom?

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:04.110
It's me.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:07.660
Oh, it's rare for you to call me.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:09.370
Has something happened?

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:13.700
Um, Mom, you knew Saito Azusa-san, right?

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:17.170
I'm going to try and explain what's happened, so listen carefully.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:23.170
They plan to kill Haruka-chan in front of Yakumo.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:25.670
Goto-san, how do you know that?

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:28.260
Takeda Shunsuke told me.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:34.600
As Yakumo would put it, Takeda is a ghost.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.900
My powers are nearing their end.

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:45.900
Therefore, I have a request to make of you.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:54.240
Just like you saved Yakumo 15 years ago, please save those two.

00:05:55.620 --> 00:06:01.380
As a ghost, Takeda has communicated with Yakumo in Nagano.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.590
Nagano is...

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:09.090
When she was young, my sister Azusa was abducted by a man

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:11.850
and held captive in a villa within the forest of Nagano.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:16.230
I see! So Haruka-chan and Yakumo-shi are in that villa.

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:27.650
Welcome home.

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:29.240
I'm home.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.570
You're in a hurry, right?

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:31.490
Get in.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:33.160
Okay.

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:46.380
Still, to think that the two of you are members of the same club.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:54.680
But will Yakumo-kun really be there?

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:56.430
I don't know...

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:01.150
but that's why I need to find out for myself.

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:05.110
Are you... possibly...

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:16.410
Wait for me here, Mom.

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:26.210
Don't be too rash, and come back the moment you think that you're in danger.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:27.170
Okay?

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:28.800
I will.

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:41.560
You always were a stubborn child.

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:56.590
Yakumo-kun!

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:02.020
He's cold.

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:05.350
Yakumo-kun, please get a hold of yourself!

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:11.110
Please open your eyes! You can't die here!

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:13.280
You're coming to my concert, remember?!

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:17.160
Isshin-san and Nao-chan are worried about you too!

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:19.320
And... so am I.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:27.210
I've still got so many things to ask you about.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.420
Yet in the end, you refuse to tell me.

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:33.460
You're still unaware of my feelings for you.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.300
And that's terrible...

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:38.970
It's unforgivable.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:43.350
Don't give up, Yakumo-kun!

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:47.940
You've got so many people waiting for you back home.

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:52.730
That's why you can never... never give up!

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:58.530
You're as... clumsy... as always.

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:03.490
I'm not dead yet.

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:06.000
Don't just kill me off like that.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:08.370
Yakumo-kun...

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:10.670
Thank goodness.

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:25.020
I've been drugged. I'm still dizzy.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:27.940
Hang in there for just a while longer, okay?

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:31.480
I don't think so.

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:44.660
Haruka...

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:54.750
Let's go.

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:03.850
Yakumo-kun...

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:16.270
Fine, I shall admit defeat.

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:19.820
However, there's still something I don't understand.

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:25.370
If the culprit of the Nanase Murders wasn't Takeda Shunsuke,

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:28.370
then who was it?

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:33.170
You really want to know?

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:38.880
The real culprit behind it all... was me.

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:40.260
What?

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:44.760
Are you saying you killed four members of your family as a child?

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:49.390
I was born from a union between my grandfather and my mother.

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:54.520
However, my father truly, truly <i>loved</i> me

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:56.520
down in that secret room.

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:58.780
You stay there.

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:00.030
But...

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:01.990
You're her bodyguard.

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:06.990
Somehow, they managed to retain their family relationship,

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:09.910
and that was mainly because of my sacrifice.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:16.000
And that's when <i>he</i> appeared.

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:22.510
And I...

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:46.620
Take a key and lock her up.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:50.990
Lock her up, lock her up.

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:54.830
Take a key and lock her up.

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:58.380
My fair lady.

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:06.890
Afterwards, <i>he</i> covered it up for me by making it look like it was all Takeda's doing.

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:11.220
Why didn't you kill the policewoman who arrived at the scene?

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:17.690
Because I needed to make people believe that Takeda held a grudge against the Nanase family.

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:19.520
I see.

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.730
I hadn't seen that far ahead either.

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:25.740
Run!

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:44.880
First, her leg.

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:47.380
I'll shatter your knee.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:20.080
Mother...

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:24.590
Azusa, do you intend to reveal everything?

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:29.840
So you're finally going to tell me?

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:42.230
This is what Takeda told me while I was being held at the Nanase residence.

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:50.490
Fifteen years ago, after Takeda met you both, he proposed to Yakumo's mother.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:54.990
However, shortly after...

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:57.000
On Screen: Four members of the Nanase family murdered.

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:02.920
For Azusa-san, who'd tried her very best to raise Yakumo despite what she'd gone through,

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:06.130
finding out that Takeda was a criminal was an enormous shock that she could not recover from.

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:11.010
And <i>he</i> caused her even further pain.

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:14.050
<i>He</i> informed her that Yakumo, who carried the same red eye as him,

00:15:14.050 --> 00:15:19.020
would eventually kill more people than Takeda had.

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:26.520
Meanwhile, he secretly killed Takeda to silence him.

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:29.570
Fear... and despair...

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:36.950
Overwhelmed by those two feelings, she... tried to kill the young Yakumo.

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:57.890
The truth will always cause pain.

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:08.440
Even if I did play a role in it, it's an undeniable fact that she tried to kill you herself.

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:11.190
I don't care.

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:20.500
My mother did not hate my red eye-
No, she did not hate me as a person.

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:24.580
As long as I know that, it's enough.

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:28.880
My mother says

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:34.510
that you gave her courage.

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:37.510
Azusa-san...

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:52.650
I've got friends who are tied to me by invisible bonds.

00:16:53.780 --> 00:16:55.910
And it's not just the living either.

00:16:57.530 --> 00:17:02.660
I can understand the feelings of ghosts.

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:05.830
I am not alone.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:11.460
Whether they're alive or dead, I have friends with whom I can share my feelings with.

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:13.300
And that's why,

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:18.430
I will not lose to you.

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:20.560
We'll see about that.

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:43.660
There are two suspects.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:46.040
They should still be close by.

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:49.170
Mom...

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:51.540
Haruka.

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:56.300
Apparently, they've found a female corpse.

00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:59.180
It's probably Yakumo-san's...

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:00.930
Yeah...

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:11.190
Ishii, can I just ask you one thing?

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:15.240
Did you find me all by yourself?

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:17.570
It was thanks to Makoto-san.

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:23.080
In addition, everyone, including Haruka-chan, helped me too.

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:25.160
I see.

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:28.670
You've matured-

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:29.790
What?

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:32.880
I-It's nothing, idiot!

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:34.550
That was just a sign of appreciation.

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:37.630
Idiot!

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:39.050
Same here.

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:43.470
If Takeda's corpse was discovered during the demolition of the house...

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:47.640
Or if his ghost had awakened to tell me the truth...

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:51.560
They were both things that <i>he</i> was especially afraid of prior to carrying out his plan.

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:55.530
But Takeda-san's ghost did appear.

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.860
It's this pendant.

00:18:58.860 --> 00:19:02.570
Takeda deeply loved my mother, so the presence of her pendant must've awakened him.

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:08.200
This is also where I was almost killed by my mother.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:11.880
I'd planned to return here one day.

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:15.090
So that's what that map was for.

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:21.010
My only impression of Takeda-san as a child was that he was a kind man.

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:28.100
I've only recently realized that Takeda-san and my mother were deeply in love with each other.

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:30.350
What made you realize that?

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:41.360
To think that Azusa-san and Takeda-san were long deceased...

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:50.370
My mother is saying,

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:53.210
"Thank you for everything."

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.670
No, thank you.

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:58.420
Sister, make sure you take care of yourself there.

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:02.550
Takeda-san, please take care of my sister.

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:08.060
"I want you to take good care of that pendant."

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:10.680
Those are my mother's words to you.

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:12.390
I will.

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:31.660
So, you're going now.

00:20:44.590 --> 00:20:45.890
Thank you,

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:49.310
Mother.

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:54.690
Oh, dear... You'll catch a cold like that.
